2026-06-03 18:56:10,349 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Attack Narrative
2026-06-03 18:56:10,351 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] The internet-facing FTP server had anonymous access enabled, allowing attackers to enumerate user directories. The attack progressed from scanning/brute force (Aug 8-31) → anonymous enumeration (Sep 2) → targeted reconnaissance by 165.227.50.129 (Sep 3, including downloading test.txt) → authenticated access as rsydow-f (Sep 5). Internal scanning from 172.16.10.13 (Nmap, Sep 4) and suspicious WebDAV access from 172.16.5.26 (Sep 7) suggest the broader network may have been compromised. Forensic response tools were staged by Sep 7.
